2. Patient Preference: Many people increasingly seek CAM for their comfort and comfort-control, such as headaches, anxiety, or nausea. Nurses are increasingly integrated in CAM training and better able to provide these CAM options.

3. Reduced Side Effects: CAPA may be used to manage side effects of conventional medications or procedures, such as fatigue, anxiety, or nausea. This can help improve patient compliance and reduce the risk of adverse effects.

