"What is the definition of whole body oxygen delivery, and how is it calculated?","<bos><start_of_turn>user
What is the definition of whole body oxygen delivery, and how is it calculated?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The definition of whole-tissue oxygen delivery is $\boxed{\text{the total amount of oxygen delivered to all tissues in the body per unit time.}}$ It is calculated using Fick's equation:  
\[
\text{VO}_2 = \dot{V} \times (F_{i} - F_{e})
\]  
where:  
- $\text{VO}_2$ is the rate of oxygen consumption (VO$_2$ in mL/min).  
- $\dot{V}$ is the rate of blood flow (in mL/min).  
- $F_{i}$ is the fraction of inspired oxygen (FiO$_2$).  
- $F_{e}$ is the fraction of end-alveolar oxygen (FaO$_2$).  

This equation is derived from the principle that the amount of oxygen delivered to the tissues is the difference between the amount of oxygen in the inspired air and the amount of oxygen in the exhaled air, multiplied by the blood flow rate.
