","The dietary condition that leads to the conversion of glucose to fatty acids in the body is **carbohydrate excess**. This occurs when the body consumes more glucose than it needs for energy production. Excess glucose is converted into fatty acids through a process called lipogenesis. This process occurs in the liver and adipose tissue. The fatty acids can then be stored as triglycerides in adipose tissue or used as energy sources by other tissues.
