3. Aromatic compounds: Aromatic compounds often undergo cleavage at the C-C bonds of the aromatic ring, leading to fragment ions with m/z values corresponding to the molecular weight minus the mass of the cleaved fragment. They may also undergo McLafferty rearrangement or other rearrangement processes.

