   C2H5OH(l) + 3O2(g) → 2CO2(g) + 3H2O(l)  ΔH = -1367 kJ/mol

2. Water combustion:
   H2O(l) + 1/2O2(g) → H2O(g)  ΔH = -285.8 kJ/mol

Now, we need to manipulate these equations to match the formation equation for ethanoic acid:

