The contribution to the tensile yield strength \(\sigma_{yr}\) of the alloy is calculated using the formula for the Hall-Oenswald rule:  
\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{G}{2} \left( \frac{b}{d} \right) \left( \frac{1}{1 + \frac{d}{d_0}} \right)
\]  
where:  
- \(G = 26 \times 10^9\) N m\(^{-2}\) (shear modulus),  
- \(b = 0.286 \times 10^{-9}\) m (Burgers vector),  
- \(d = 10^{-8}\) m (particle diameter),  
- \(d_0 = 6 \times 10^{-8}\) m (average center-to-center spacing).  

