   \[
   0.56 = 1 - \frac{1}{R^{1.4 - 1}}
   \]
   Solving for \( R \):
   \[
   R = \left( \frac{1}{1 - 0.56} \right)^{1/0.4} = 2.63
   \]

2. **Work Done (W)**:
   The work done per kg of air is related to the heat rejected (\( Q_R \)) and the efficiency:
   \[
   W = \eta \cdot Q_R = 0.56 \times 544 = 300.24 \, \text{kJ/kg}
